## Summary
In `codex-rs/core/src/session/turn_context.rs` (`TurnContext::with_model`), when switching to a model whose `supported_reasoning_levels` does not directly contain the current `reasoning_effort` (or when `self.reasoning_effort()` is `None`), `with_model` computes:

```rust
supported_reasoning_levels
    .get(supported_reasoning_levels.len().saturating_sub(1) / 2)
    .cloned()
    .or_else(|| model_info.default_reasoning_level.clone())
```

This causes two regressions:
1. When switching from a model configured with `Max` or `Ultra` reasoning effort to a model supporting `[Low, Medium, High, XHigh]` (such as `gpt-5.5`), `(4 - 1) / 2 == 1` selects `Medium` instead of clamping to the highest supported non-`Ultra` preset (`XHigh`).
2. Because `.or_else(|| model_info.default_reasoning_level.clone())` is only evaluated when `supported_reasoning_levels` is empty, `model_info.default_reasoning_level` (for example `Some(High)`) is ignored whenever `supported_reasoning_levels` is non-empty.

## Expected Behavior
- Add `ModelInfo::resolve_reasoning_effort_for_model_switch(&self, current_effort: Option<&ReasoningEffort>) -> Option<ReasoningEffort>` in `codex-protocol`.
- Preserve `current_effort` when directly supported; resolve `Ultra` via `ModelInfo::resolve_reasoning_effort`; clamp higher ordered efforts (`Max`, `XHigh`, etc.) to the highest supported non-`Ultra` preset `<= current_effort`; and otherwise prefer a supported `default_reasoning_level` before falling back to the median preset.

## Environment
- Codex CLI version: `0.162.1` (`aarch64-apple-darwin`)
- Codex Desktop version: `26.1007.71326` (embedded CLI `0.162.0-alpha.17.2`)
- OS: macOS `aarch64`

## Root-Cause Analysis & Verification

## Summary
- Adds `ModelInfo::resolve_reasoning_effort_for_model_switch` in `codex-rs/protocol/src/openai_models/reasoning_effort.rs`.
- Updates `TurnContext::with_model` in `codex-rs/core/src/session/turn_context.rs` to delegate reasoning effort resolution on model switches to `model_info.resolve_reasoning_effort_for_model_switch(self.reasoning_effort())`.
- Preserves existing request-level `ModelInfo::resolve_reasoning_effort` semantics while clamping unsupported high efforts (e.g. `Max` -> `XHigh` on `gpt-5.5`) and honoring `default_reasoning_level` ahead of the median preset fallback.

## Verification
- `cargo test --offline -p codex-protocol reasoning_effort` (7 passed)
- `cargo test --offline -p codex-core --lib turn_context_with_model_updates_model_fields` (passed)
- `cargo test --offline -p codex-core --lib reasoning_effort_for_requests_preserves_non_ultra_and_persistent_behavior` (passed)
- `cargo clippy --offline -p codex-protocol --all-targets --no-deps -- -D warnings` (0 warnings)

